$COST — 

In May, refund claims filed, no dollar attached, returns expected &quot;on a rolling basis.&quot; 
This quarter: $184M received ($174M refunds, $10M interest), &quot;a little more than one-third&quot; of total expected. 
Price cuts followed in produce, meat, beverages, home furnishings, and hardware — unit growth described as &quot;fantastic.&quot; 

Against that: eight consecutive quarters of decelerating membership growth, now at 3.8%. 
Core-on-core margins up 18bps, broad-based.
